## Accessibility & i18n

### Semantic structure
- Rendered tag: `<div>` (generic container, no implicit role)
- Marker: `<span class="marker">` (visual only, not structural)
- Title: `<h3>` (semantic heading hierarchy)
- Body: `<p>` or `<body>` (semantic paragraphs)
- Full structure announced by screen readers as nested headings + paragraphs

### RTL / i18n
- English-only? (e.g., [ADR-0003: ISSA Landing English-only](../docs/adr/0003-...))
- If multilingual: logical properties used (not `left`/`right`), margins/padding flex with `dir="rtl"`
- If RTL: marker position mirrored?

### Localization
- Dates in meta: format (e.g., "2026-2027" assumes English, may need i18n formatting for other locales)
- No hardcoded strings in component (content comes from props)

## Scope & Constraints

### What this component does
- Renders a two-column timeline entry (marker + content)
- Handles responsive collapse below 600px
- Projects arbitrary content via `children`

### What this component does NOT do
- Validate marker/meta/title content (caller's responsibility)
- Manage timeline list state (parent owns the list)
- Scroll or animate (static layout only)
- Assign semantic meaning to marker (e.g., "this is phase 01" — that's up to caller)

### Reusability boundary
- **Feature-local, not design-system**: This component is tightly coupled to Mission+Program section's visual story. Not intended for reuse in other apps or sections.
- **Reason**: Coupling to specific scroll-linked motion (if applicable), layout grid proportions that assume page context.
- **If moving to design-system**: Decouple scroll bindings, generalize prop names, add Storybook stories.

### Dependencies
- No external primitives (Radix, react-aria, etc.)
- No state management (Zustand, Redux, etc.)
- CSS Modules only

